# LeakSanitizer suppressions for running LightMem tests under Python + PyTorch.
#
# Rationale:
# - CPython and libtorch/pybind11 keep global caches and allocations that are
#   intentionally not freed at process exit. With `detect_leaks=1`, these show
#   up as leaks and can cause test runs to abort.
# - These suppressions aim to reduce noise so leaks in LightMem's C++ code are
#   easier to spot.
#
# Notes:
# - Suppressions match by symbol name in the leak stack.
# - Keep this file minimal; avoid overly broad patterns if possible.

# CPython allocator / unicode internals (common shutdown leaks)
leak:_PyMem_RawMalloc
leak:_PyObject_Malloc
leak:PyObject_Malloc
leak:_PyObject_New
leak:PyUnicode_New
leak:PyFloat_FromDouble

# CPython GC allocation helpers
leak:_PyObject_GC_Alloc
leak:_PyObject_GC_Malloc
leak:_PyObject_GC_NewVar

# pybind11 function record allocations (often kept for module lifetime)
leak:pybind11::cpp_function::make_function_record

# PyTorch binding init (pybind registrations)
leak:torch::jit::initJITBindings
